=== 3. One-to-One Correspondence: The Bag of Pebbles
<one-to-one-correspondence-the-bag-of-pebbles>
Let us return to our prehistoric shepherd. The sun rises, and the sheep
are pawing at the gate. Here is the stroke of genius he invents:

+ He picks up an empty leather pouch and hangs it from his belt.
+ He opens the thornwood gate just enough to let the sheep pass
  #strong[one by one].
+ The first sheep walks out? The shepherd picks up a small pebble and
  drops it into his pouch: #emph[Plop!]
+ The second sheep walks out? Another pebble goes into the pouch:
  #emph[Plop!]
+ Every single time an animal crosses the threshold, #strong[one pebble
  and only one] enters the bag.

When the last sheep bounds onto the hill, the shepherd pulls the
drawstring closed. He still does not know the number of his sheep. Yet
he knows something monumental: #strong[there are in his bag exactly as
many pebbles as there are living animals on the hill!] Every pebble is
the secret twin of a sheep.

