=== 5. From the Pebble to the Carved Tally: The Ishango Bone
<from-the-pebble-to-the-carved-tally-the-ishango-bone>
The bag of pebbles has one major flaw: if your flock grows to 80 sheep,
your pouch becomes as heavy as a boulder and tears your belt.

Our ancestors therefore devised a much lighter tool: #strong[the tally
stick]. Each time an animal passes, one strikes a sharp flint against a
polished bone or flat piece of wood: #emph[Scritch!]

