=== The Question That Opens the Journey Ahead…
<the-question-that-opens-the-journey-ahead>
You are now able to track and verify any collection of objects using a
pouch of pebbles or carved notches on a bone.

Yet imagine that your settlement expands. You no longer herd six sheep,
but #strong[three hundred]! And the miller has harvested thousands of
wheat grains in his sacks.

If you had to carry three hundred pebbles in your pouch, it would weigh
so much that you could barely walk! And if you tried to carve three
thousand notches on a bone, it would snap in half.

How did humans learn to count very large numbers without collapsing
under the weight of stones? The answer is magnificent: they simply
looked down at #strong[the ends of their arms]!

See you in #strong[Chapter 2: The Five-Fingered Hand and Bundles of
Ten]!

