=== The Question That Opens the Next Chapter…
<the-question-that-opens-the-next-chapter-1>
You now know how to measure lengths, weigh objects, tell time, and make
change with money.

Yet have you looked closely at the shapes of the stones forming houses?
Some have four straight sides and crisp corners: rectangles and squares.
Others are pointed like pyramids, circular like the sun, or cubic like a
rolling die.

How did master builders learn to trace a flawless circle on the ground
using only a simple string and two pegs? And how does a folded sheet of
paper bring forth a magical butterfly?

