== CHAPTER 7: The Shapes of the World and the Gardener's String
<chapter-7-the-shapes-of-the-world-and-the-gardeners-string>
#quote_box[
#emph[“Look around you: the Earth does not speak solely in numbers, it
speaks in shapes. Tree trunks are cylinders, honeycombs are hexagons,
and river-polished stones are spheres. To trace a straight figure in the
sand is to begin drawing the world.”
]

]

#divider()

=== What You Are About to Discover
<what-you-are-about-to-discover-6>
- How to recognize plane figures all around you: the #strong[square],
  the #strong[rectangle], the #strong[triangle], and the
  #strong[circle].
- The secret of the gardener's string: tracing a flawless circle without
  a compass using two wooden pegs.
- Entering the three-dimensional world: solids (the #strong[cube], the
  #strong[rectangular prism], the #strong[sphere], the
  #strong[cylinder]).
- The vocabulary of builders: #strong[vertex], #strong[face], and
  #strong[edge].
- Using a ruler and crafting a #strong[folded-paper set square] to test
  right angles.
- The magic of the mirror and the paper butterfly: the #strong[axis of
  symmetry].
- Navigating a grid and programming a robot's path with step-by-step
  arrows.

