=== What You Are About to Discover
<what-you-are-about-to-discover-7>
- What #strong[multiples] of a number are (the numbers you land on when
  always leaping by the same length).
- What #strong[divisors] of a number are (row lengths that divide evenly
  with nothing left over).
- #strong[Detective tricks] to know, without calculating long divisions,
  whether a number divides evenly by 2, 3, 5, 9, or 10.
- #strong[Prime numbers], those numbers that refuse to form rectangles,
  and why they are the bricks of all other numbers.
- The #strong[Sieve of Eratosthenes], a number-sorting machine invented
  more than 2,000 years ago.

