=== What You Need to Remember
<what-you-need-to-remember>
+ #strong[Euclidean division] is used to divide a whole quantity into
  equal parts or to count how many full groups can be formed.
+ #strong[The 4 actors:]
  $ upright("Dividend") =\(upright("Divisor") times upright("Quotient")\)+ upright("Remainder") $
  $ a =\(b times q\)+ r $
+ #strong[The mandatory golden rule:] The remainder must always be
  strictly less than the divisor: $ 0 lt.eq r < b $
+ #strong[Long division layout:] We process digits from left to right
  following the cycle: #emph[Divide $arrow.r$ Multiply $arrow.r$
  Subtract $arrow.r$ Bring down].
+ #strong[Zero in the quotient:] Whenever you bring down a digit and
  cannot form a group, you must write a `0` in the quotient before
  bringing down the next digit.
+ #strong[Verification:] Always verify using $\(b times q\)+ r$.

