sturgeons. And #strong[2 large fish] remained on the stone table.

The families are still hungry. The children look at these two remaining
fish with longing. The village elder declares: #emph[“These two fish
must not be wasted! Since we cannot distribute them whole, we will draw
the sharp knife and slice them into equal parts!”]

But when we break a whole object into pieces, how do we name these
parts? How do we write with numbers a part that is smaller than 1? That
is the great leap into the next chapter: #strong[The Broken Galette and
the Measuring Sieve]!

