=== What You Are About to Discover
<what-you-are-about-to-discover-12>
- How to adapt any #strong[cooking recipe] without ever spoiling its
  taste.
- How to recognize a genuine situation of #strong[proportionality] and
  spot false ones (no, you will not be 10 feet tall at age 20!).
- How to organize information into a clean, crystal-clear
  #strong[proportionality table].
- The three classic calculation methods:
  + The #strong[column-jumping method] (doubling, tripling, adding
    columns).
  + The #strong[unit rate method] (finding the price of a single item).
  + The #strong[constant of proportionality] (the direct vertical
    multiplier).
- The secret behind the famous #strong[“rule of three”], the ancient
  merchants' shortcut explained without mystery.
