=== What You Are About to Discover
<what-you-are-about-to-discover-13>
- Why #strong[zero is not pure nothingness], but a reference level and a
  point of equilibrium.
- The physical model of the #strong[sand heap and sand pit]: how matter
  and hollow cancel each other out ($\(+ 1\)+\(- 1\)= 0$).
- Elevators, underground parking levels ($- 1\,- 2$), depth below sea
  level, and #strong[winter thermometers].
- The #strong[complete number line]: crossing the zero border and
  venturing leftward.
- How to compare negative numbers without stumbling: understanding why
  #strong[$- 5$ is smaller than $- 2$] (the colder it is, the lower the
  number!).
- #strong[Adding negative numbers]: filling pits and accumulating debts.
- Calculating #strong[temperature intervals] and elevation differences.

