=== 2. What Is an Angle?
<what-is-an-angle>
==== 2.1 The Intuition with Your Own Body
<the-intuition-with-your-own-body>
Extend your right arm straight out in front of you, perfectly
horizontal. Keep your shoulder pinned in place and slowly pivot your arm
to your right, like the hand of a clock sweeping across a dial.

- At first, your arm has barely moved: the #strong[opening] between your
  starting direction and your current direction is narrow.
- When your arm points straight out to your right side, it has made a
  #strong[quarter-turn]: this is a right angle.
- If you keep pivoting until your arm points straight behind you, you
  have completed a #strong[half-turn].
- And if you pivot all the way back to the front, you have made a
  #strong[full turn].

This is the essence of an angle: #strong[the amount of rotation between
two directions that originate from the same common point]. Your shoulder
acts as the #strong[vertex], and the two pointing directions are its two
#strong[sides] (rays).

==== 2.2 Words, Notations, and Geometrical Symbols
<words-notations-and-geometrical-symbols>
Before proceeding further, let us recall the foundational notation of
geometry:

