=== The Question That Opens What Follows
<the-question-that-opens-what-follows>
We now know how to master straight lines, perpendiculars, and the sharp
angles of polygons. But what happens when the lines begin to curve and
sweep smoothly through space without a single corner?

In the dark corner of an ancient artisan's workshop, a heavy wooden disc
spins smoothly upon an iron pivot: the #strong[potter's wheel]. How can
one measure the curved rim of a circle when no ruler can bend around it
without slipping? And what is this infinite, mysterious number that the
great #strong[Archimedes of Syracuse] tracked down between two vast
armies of polygons? That is the secret of the circle and the number
$pi$, which we shall unveil in the next chapter.

