== CHAPTER 16: The Potter's Wheel and Archimedes' Secret
<chapter-16-the-potters-wheel-and-archimedes-secret>
#quote_box[
#emph[“Every polygon built of right angles readily submits to a grid.
But the gentle curve of the circle slips through the surveyor's fingers.
To measure the perfect ring, one had to unroll the circumference upon
the earth and discover that mysterious, unending number without
repetition that the sages of Syracuse hunted down between two vast
armies of polygons.”
]

]

