=== The Question That Opens What Follows
<the-question-that-opens-what-follows-1>
We now know how to measure round, curving shapes upon the ground. But
what can we do when the object to be measured is neither a small wheel
before our eyes nor a cord we can lay across the sand, but a towering
mountain of stone: the #strong[Great Pyramid of Giza]?

How did a Greek philosopher named #strong[Thales], armed with nothing
more than a simple wooden stick planted in the scorching desert sand,
deduce the exact height of the greatest tomb on Earth without ever
climbing a single step? That is the secret of #strong[geometric
proportions and similar triangles], which we shall master in the next
chapter.

