=== 1. The Problem: The Pharaoh's Insolent Challenge
<the-problem-the-pharaohs-insolent-challenge>
The desert wind whips up golden dust swirls across the Giza plateau in
Egypt, twenty-six hundred years ago. Before you looms the Great Pyramid
of Pharaoh Khufu: an artificial mountain of solid limestone soaring to a
dizzying height.

Pharaoh Amasis gathers his high priests, court architects, and surveyors
at the foot of the stone giant: #emph[“Who among you is wise enough to
determine the exact vertical height of this sacred tomb, from the
bedrock of the earth to the gilded peak that touches the sky?”]

The master builders lower their eyes in embarrassment: #emph[“Your
Majesty, the four faces are polished smooth as glass and slope steeply
toward the heavens. No man can climb with a surveyor's measuring chain
without slipping and falling one hundred and forty meters to his
death!”]

A foreign traveler, hailing from the Greek city of Miletus and cloaked
in a simple woolen mantle, steps calmly forward. His name is
#strong[Thales]. Thales gazes up at the stone colossus, observes the
blazing sun in the azure sky, and smiles: #emph[“Your Majesty, I have no
need to climb your pyramid. Hand me a simple wooden walking staff, and
before sunset, I shall give you the exact height of the monument without
ever lifting my feet from the ground!”]

The Egyptian courtiers scoff. How could an itinerant Greek merchant
measure a stone mountain with a common piece of wood?

