=== The Question That Opens What Follows
<the-question-that-opens-what-follows-2>
When we scale a 3D pyramid or cube, its volume multiplies by $k^3$: it
explodes upward at tremendous speed. But what happens when we do not
merely triple a dimension once, but repeat a multiplication dozens of
times in succession?

It is the legend of an Eastern king who thought he was granting a humble
handful of rice to the inventor of chess, only to discover his entire
empire buried beneath a mountain of grain. Welcome to the dizzying
universe of #strong[exponents, order of operations, and scientific
notation]!

