=== The Question That Opens What Follows
<the-question-that-opens-what-follows-3>
We now know that $a^2$ represents the square of a number: $3^2 = 9$,
$4^2 = 16$. But what happens when we attempt the reverse operation? What
number multiplied by itself yields exactly $2$?

This innocent question shattered the most secret philosophical
brotherhood of ancient Greece, sparked death sentences on the open sea,
and revealed a terrifying breed of numbers that no fraction can tame:
#strong[irrational numbers]. Step into the mystic sanctuary of Croton
with #strong[The Pythagorean Theorem]!

