=== 4. The Square Root: Journeying Backward from Square to Side
<the-square-root-journeying-backward-from-square-to-side>
When using the Pythagorean Theorem to find an unknown side length, we
typically compute $c^2$ (the area of the square), and need to find $c$
(the side length). To do so, we introduce a fundamental mathematical
tool: #strong[the radical symbol for square roots].

