=== The Question That Opens What Follows
<the-question-that-opens-what-follows-4>
The Pythagorean Theorem allows us to calculate the diagonal
straight-line distance between two points. But what happens when our
points are not drawn upon a free blank sheet of paper, but scattered
across a navigator's nautical chart, a pirate's treasure map, or the
pixel grid of a computer screen?

How can we pinpoint any location on Earth with absolute accuracy using
two signed numbers, positive or negative? And why does “minus times
minus equal plus”? That is the secret of #strong[René Descartes and the
two trails of Treasure Island]!

