=== What You Are About to Discover
<what-you-are-about-to-discover-19>
- The mystery of the pirate's map and the legendary fly on the ceiling
  of #strong[René Descartes].
- The #strong[Cartesian coordinate plane]: the horizontal
  #strong[$x$-axis] of abscissas, the vertical #strong[$y$-axis] of
  ordinates, and the #strong[four quadrants].
- How to plot and read the #strong[coordinates] of a point
  $\(x thin\;thin y\)$ without ever reversing them.
- The formula for the #strong[midpoint of a segment]: the simple
  arithmetic average of coordinates.
- Calculating the exact #strong[distance between two points] in a
  coordinate plane via the Pythagorean Theorem:
  $A B = sqrt(\(x_B - x_A\)^2 +\(y_B - y_A\)^2)$.
- #strong[Multiplication and division of signed (relative) numbers]: why
  “negative times negative equals positive,” proved through
  time-reversed motion and algebraic distributivity!
- 🛠️ The Boundary Case Laboratory: points on the axes, reflections
  across the origin, and irrational coordinates in Euclidean space.

