3 |            :
2 |            :
1 |            :
Right Wall (Horizontal x-axis)
O   1   2    3    4    5
Room Corner
    ```
  ]
]

Descartes looks at the two perpendicular walls meeting in the corner of
his bedroom: 1. He measures the horizontal distance from the fly to the
#strong[left wall]: say, #strong[3 meters]. 2. He measures the vertical
distance from the fly to the #strong[far wall]: say, #strong[4 meters].

#emph[“It is luminous!”] Descartes realizes. The ordered pair of numbers
$\(3 thin\;thin 4\)$ uniquely fixes the position of the fly upon the
flat ceiling without the slightest ambiguity! Two numbers to identify
any point in a two-dimensional world: Descartes had just invented the
#strong[Cartesian coordinate system].

