=== The Question That Opens What Follows
<the-question-that-opens-what-follows-5>
With Cartesian coordinates, we can locate any individual point or buried
chest across space. Yet what happens when a tax collector must levy fair
contributions from hundreds of merchants of wildly differing wealth, or
when a school must summarize the test scores of an entire class in a
single representative figure?

How do we compare portions fairly when group totals are never the same?
That is the power of #strong[percentages], and the birth of
#strong[statistics]---with means, medians, and frequency diagrams---in
our final chapter!

