=== What You Must Remember
<what-you-must-remember-6>
+ #strong[Percentage Concepts:]

  - $t % = t / 100$.

  - Calculate $p %$ of $Q$: $Q times p / 100$.

  - Find percentage rate:
    $upright("Part") / upright("Total") times 100$.

+ #strong[Multiplier Coefficients:]

  - Increase of $t %$: multiply by $(1 + t / 100)$.

  - Decrease of $t %$: multiply by $(1 - t / 100)$.

  - Consecutive changes: #strong[multiply] coefficients
    ($C_(upright("total")) = C_1 times C_2$).

+ #strong[Statistical Indicators:]

  - #strong[Relative Frequency:] $f = upright("count") / N$.

  - #strong[Pie Chart Angle:] $upright("Angle") = f times 360^compose$.

  - #strong[Mean ($macron(x)$):] sum of all values divided by total
    count $N$.

  - #strong[Median ($M e$):] the midpoint value dividing sorted data
    into equal $50 %\/50 %$ halves.

  - #strong[Range ($R$):]
    $upright("maximum value") - upright("minimum value")$.

#divider()

