#set enum(numbering: "1.", start: 3)
+ Dr.~Martin has an overall success rate of $87.5 %$ versus $53.3 %$ for
  Dr.~Dupont! The paradox: for routine cases, both surgeons have
  identical success rates ($95 %$). For high-risk cases, Dr.~Martin is
  superior ($50 %$ vs.~$45 %$). And overall, Dr.~Martin dramatically
  outperforms Dr.~Dupont! Explanation: Dr.~Martin performed $83 %$ of
  his surgeries on easy, low-risk patients, whereas Dr.~Dupont took on
  $83 %$ high-risk, dangerous operations. This famous statistical
  phenomenon is known as #strong[Simpson's Paradox]: an unobserved
  confounding variable (the underlying severity of cases) distorts the
