=== The Question That Opens What Follows
<the-question-that-opens-what-follows-6>
We have arrived at the conclusion of Volume III. We now know how to
measure the earth, lay out right angles with compass and rope, compute
inaccessible heights with Thales and Pythagoras, navigate Cartesian
planes with signed coordinates, and synthesize crowds of data with
percentages and statistics.

Yet up to this point, all our numbers were known, or uncovered through
direct arithmetic. What happens when a problem hides a secret unknown
quantity inside a sealed velvet bag resting upon a balance scale,
tangled in a web of additions and multiplications?

How do we forge a new mathematical language where unknown numbers are
represented by letters like $x$, and where the scales of justice
transform into algebraic equations? That is the great threshold into the
adolescence of mathematics: #strong[Volume IV and the Mystery Bag on the
Balance of Al-Khwarizmi]!

