$ \(a - b\)\(a^2 + a b + b^2\)= a times a^2 + a times a b + a times b^2 - b times a^2 - b times a b - b times b^2 $
$ = a^3 + a^2 b + a b^2 - a^2 b - a b^2 - b^3 . $ All intermediate terms
cancel pairwise! $ = a^3 - b^3 . $ 2. We observe that the difference of
two cubes factors according to the remarkable formula:
$ a^3 - b^3 =\(a - b\)\(a^2 + a b + b^2\). $ 3. For
$x^3 - 8 = x^3 - 2^3$, apply with $a = x$ and $b = 2$:
$ x^3 - 8 =\(x - 2\)\(x^2 + 2 x + 2^2\)=\(x - 2\)\(x^2 + 2 x + 4\). $

