=== The Question Opening the Next Chapter
<the-question-opening-the-next-chapter>
Thanks to special products and the zero-product property, you now know
how to master perfect equalities and strict balance. But in real life
and commerce, scale pans rarely rest at the exact same level: one is
often heavier than the other, a subscription price becomes more
advantageous than another beyond a certain threshold, and two merchants
compete for customers.

What happens when the scale tilts? How can we manipulate an
#strong[inequality] without turning the world upside down, and how do we
determine the intersection of two merchant destinies? That is the
mystery we will unravel in the next chapter: #strong[The Two Merchants
and Inequalities].

