=== The Question Opening the Next Chapter
<the-question-opening-the-next-chapter-2>
Thus far, numbers have served to calculate weights, prices, areas, and
linear trajectories. But look around you: a repeating fabric pattern,
roof tiles, a six-petaled flower, the infinite mosaics of the Alhambra
in Granada, or the dizzying art of M. C. Escher.

How can a single triangle or shape #strong[slide], #strong[rotate],
#strong[reflect across a mirror], or #strong[expand under a magnifying
glass] while preserving its exact proportions? That is the enchanting
realm of plane transformations that we will explore in Chapter 26:
#strong[Paper Folding and the Magic Mirror].

