=== What You Are About to Discover
<what-you-are-about-to-discover-25>
- The secret of medieval master builders: why asymmetry tears down stone
  bridges, and how the #strong[perpendicular bisector] and #strong[angle
  bisector] produce geometric harmony.
- The grand family of plane geometric transformations:
  - #strong[Axial reflection (line symmetry)]: paper folding and the
    mirror image.

  - #strong[Point reflection (central symmetry)]: the perfect half-turn
    ($180^compose$) around a pivot.

  - #strong[Translation]: rectilinear sliding without the slightest
    rotation.

  - #strong[Rotation]: controlled whirling through a given angle around
    a center.

  - #strong[Dilation (homothety)]: the optical zoom lens shrinking or
    expanding space by a scale factor $k$.
- The properties these transformations #strong[preserve]: lengths,
  angles, parallelism, and areas.
- The vital distinction between #strong[congruent triangles] (identical
  clones) and #strong[similar triangles] (identical silhouette at
  different scales).
- The enchanting art of #strong[friezes and tessellations]: from the
  arabesques of the Alhambra in Granada to the impossible metamorphoses
  of Maurits Cornelis Escher.

