=== 1. The Problem: The Collapsing Bridge and the Well Dispute
<the-problem-the-collapsing-bridge-and-the-well-dispute>
In the 12th century, within a steep gorge of the Auvergne mountains,
local villagers decided to construct a massive stone arch bridge across
a roaring river. The master mason was in a hurry: he cut unequal
voussoirs and erected an arch leaning noticeably to the right, much
heavier on one flank than the other. The arch was picturesque, but
dangerously unbalanced.

A few months later, the first heavy autumn flood arrived. The torrent
surged, and howling winds rushed through the ravine. The heavier side
pulled relentlessly upon the thinner side. A winding crack snaked across
the vault… and with a deafening roar of crushed masonry, #strong[the
bridge collapsed into the abyss]!

#figure(image("figures/vol_4/fig_22_balance_al_khwarizmi.svg", alt: "La balance d’Al-Khwarizmi et l’équilibre des équations"),
  caption: [
    La balance d'Al-Khwarizmi et l'équilibre des équations
  ]
)

The master builder summoned his apprentices around his drafting table:
#emph[“Carve this into your memories: stone forgives surface roughness,
but it never forgives asymmetry. When an arch lacks its mirror axis, the
weight of the heavens bears down on a single abutment, and ruin is
certain.”]

A few leagues away, another dispute arose between two neighboring
villages, Arras and Béthune, separated by six kilometers of open heath.
The local count decided to sink a large stone well in the plain to water
livestock and travelers.

Instantly, discord erupted: #emph[“Dig the well right near our church
bell tower!”] demanded the villagers of Arras. #emph[“Out of the
question!”] retorted the folk of Béthune. #emph[“That would be blatant
favoritism! We insist that the walking distance be strictly equal for
both villages!”]

A child suggested: #emph[“Let us dig the well right in the middle of the
footpath connecting the two villages!”] That was a sound idea: at 3
kilometers from Arras and 3 kilometers from Béthune, the location was
fair. Yet the commander's surveyor stepped forward and scored a deep
trench across the soil with his spear: #emph[“There is not merely one
possible location: there are infinitely many fair locations for the
well!”]

