Look at the extraordinary journey we have accomplished: we know how to
dissect shapes, compute areas, manipulate equations, inequalities, and
functions. But what happens when we leave the flat sheet of paper and
step into the three-dimensional depth of our physical universe? How do
we measure the capacity of a conical amphora, a stone pyramid, or planet
Earth itself?

That is the grand exploration of space, solids, and cross sections
awaiting you in the next chapter: #strong[Land Partitioning and the
Potter's Box].

