=== 6. The Two Primary Problems in Middle School Trigonometry
<the-two-primary-problems-in-middle-school-trigonometry>
Every middle school trigonometry problem boils down to one of two
quests: 1. #strong[Calculate an unknown length] when given an angle and
another side length. 2. #strong[Calculate an unknown angle] when given
two side lengths.

Here is the 4-step method:

#align(center)[
  #block(
    fill: rgb("#f8fafc"),
    stroke: 1pt + rgb("#cbd5e1"),
    inset: (x: 16pt, y: 10pt),
    radius: 6pt,
    breakable: false,
  )[
    #set text(font: "Liberation Mono", size: 9.5pt, fill: rgb("#0f172a"))
    ```text
1. Sketch a diagram and identify the right
angle and the target acute angle.
2. Label the three sides:
Hypotenuse / Adjacent / Opposite.
3. Select the correct formula:
Adjacent and Hypotenuse? => CAH
Opposite and Hypotenuse? => SOH
Opposite and Adjacent?   => TOA
4. Write the equation, isolate the unknown
cross-multiply), and evaluate.
    ```
  ]
]

