=== What You Are About to Discover
<what-you-are-about-to-discover-28>
- Why certain numbers refuse to be factored and constitute the
  #strong[atoms of arithmetic]: prime numbers.
- How to factor any positive integer into a #strong[unique product of
  prime factors] using factor trees and successive division ladders.
- What the #strong[GCD (Greatest Common Divisor)] is, and three distinct
  methods to compute it.
- The dazzling insight conceived by #strong[Euclid] over twenty-three
