]

How can we resolve both dilemmas without spending three weeks testing
random numbers? In both cases, the underlying mathematical challenge is
identical: we seek an integer that #strong[evenly divides] two numbers
simultaneously, and which is #strong[as large as possible].

To enlighten the artisans, a scholar steps into the palace courtyard
carrying the papyrus rolls of his masterpiece, the #emph[Elements]. His
name is #strong[Euclid].

