=== What You Are About to Discover
<what-you-are-about-to-discover-29>
- How to transform the fog of uncertainty into a #strong[precise number
  between 0 and 1] (the probability).
- The formal vocabulary that structures chance: #strong[random
  experiment], #strong[outcome], #strong[event], #strong[certain,
  impossible, and complementary events].
- Why the formula
  $P\(E\)= upright("number of favorable outcomes") / upright("number of possible outcomes")$
  only works under #strong[equiprobability], and the monumental pitfall
  of the two dice.
- How to explore the two-stage future using a #strong[probability tree
  diagram] and a #strong[two-way table].
- The crucial difference between sampling #strong[with replacement] and
  sampling #strong[without replacement].
- How real-world chance obeys the law of large numbers: the
  #strong[stabilization of relative frequencies] and computer
  simulation.

