- #strong[The Marsh Trail (Path A):] It is a flat track, easy on the
  animals' feet. But the region is riddled with treacherous mud pits.
  Merchant records show that out of 100 caravans that took this trail
  this year, #strong[10 became bogged down and lost everything], while
  90 arrived safe and sound.
- #strong[The Gorge Trail (Path B):] It is a steep, rocky defile, twice
  as short and much faster. But armed bandits lurk in the caves: out of
  100 caravans, #strong[40 were ambushed and plundered], while 60
  managed to cross unscathed.

The young camel driver exclaims: #emph[“Let us take the gorge trail! We
will arrive tomorrow at dawn to sell at the best price! With a bit of
luck, the bandits will be asleep!”]

The old leader shakes his head: #emph[“Luck is not a prayer one casts
into the sky. Luck is a fraction of reality. He who cannot weigh risk
walks blindfolded toward the abyss!”]

For the first time in the history of mathematics, we are no longer
merely measuring what lies before our eyes (a length, a weight, a count
of tiles), but #strong[what has not yet happened]! We enter the realm of
#strong[Probability].

