=== The Question That Opens the Future
<the-question-that-opens-the-future>
Here ends our grand journey through Middle School (#emph[Collège]). You
began with the mystery of Al-Khwarizmi's letters, balanced scale pans,
conquered the Pythagorean Theorem, measured the Earth with Eratosthenes,
unlocked the secrets of Euclid, and learned to tame uncertainty with
Pascal and Fermat.

Yet an immense frontier now stands before you. Until now, our numbers
were either discrete counters on fingers or static lengths locked within
stationary figures. What happens when the wind blows, when a sailboat
battles the crosscurrent in the heart of a storm? How can we represent a
force that pulls in a specific direction with a precise magnitude?
Welcome to High School (#emph[Lycée]): in Volume V, numbers will take
flight, grow arrows, soar into the sky, and become #strong[vectors].

