=== Key Takeaways
<key-takeaways-13>
+ #strong[Vector:] a geometric entity characterized by a
  #strong[direction] (line of action), a #strong[sense] (arrowhead), and
  a #strong[magnitude/norm] (length $parallel arrow(u) parallel$).

+ #strong[Vector Equality:]
  $accent(A B, ⃗) = accent(C D, ⃗) arrow.l.r.double A B D C$ is a
  parallelogram.

+ #strong[Chasles' Relation:]
  $accent(A B, ⃗) + accent(B C, ⃗) = accent(A C, ⃗)$. To subtract:
  $arrow(u) - arrow(v) = arrow(u) +\(- arrow(v)\)$ where
  $- accent(A B, ⃗) = accent(B A, ⃗)$.

+ #strong[Midpoint $I$ of $\[A B\]$:]
  $accent(A I, ⃗) = accent(I B, ⃗) arrow.l.r.double accent(I A, ⃗) + accent(I B, ⃗) = arrow(0) arrow.l.r.double accent(M A, ⃗) + accent(M B, ⃗) = 2 accent(M I, ⃗)$.

+ #strong[Coordinates:]

  - $accent(A B, ⃗) vec(x_B - x_A, y_B - y_A)$

  - Midpoint: $I (frac(x_A + x_B, 2) thin \; thin frac(y_A + y_B, 2))$

  - Norm: $parallel arrow(u) parallel = sqrt(x^2 + y^2)$ and
    $A B = sqrt(\(x_B - x_A\)^2 +\(y_B - y_A\)^2)$ (in an orthonormal
    frame).

+ #strong[Collinearity and Determinant:]

  - $arrow(u)$ and $arrow(v)$ are collinear
    $arrow.l.r.double arrow(u) = k arrow(v)$ (or one is zero)
    $arrow.l.r.double det\(arrow(u)\,arrow(v)\)= x y' - y x' = 0$.

  - Parallel lines:
    $\(A B\)parallel\(C D\)arrow.l.r.double det\(accent(A B, ⃗)\,accent(C D, ⃗)\)= 0$.

  - Collinear points: $A\,B\,C$ collinear
    $arrow.l.r.double det\(accent(A B, ⃗)\,accent(A C, ⃗)\)= 0$.

