=== The Question That Opens the Future
<the-question-that-opens-the-future-1>
We have learned to slide free arrows throughout the plane and to detect
whether two arrows point along the same line using the determinant. But
what happens when we drive a stake into the ground at point $A$ and let
arrow $arrow(u)$ point out an infinite trajectory? We obtain a
#strong[straight line].

How can we characterize the set of all points aligned along this line of
sight? How do we link the algebraic equation of a line to its direction
vectors, and how do we calculate the exact location where two
trajectories intersect? That is what we will discover in #strong[The
Line of Sight].

