=== The Question That Opens the Future
<the-question-that-opens-the-future-2>
A straight line represents mathematics in its most well-behaved and
predictable form: a relationship where every step forward produces the
exact same steady return. This is the domain of affine functions
$x mapsto m x + p$.

Yet what happens when the inner rule of the machine becomes more
intricate? When the machine squares numbers, reciprocates them, or
extracts square roots? How do we map the curves, crests, and valleys of
non-linear graphs? That is what we are about to explore in #strong[The
Jacquard Loom and the Function Box].

