=== What You Are About to Discover
<what-you-are-about-to-discover-33>
- How the invention of punched cards by #strong[Joseph Marie Jacquard]
  in Lyon and the brilliant insight of #strong[Ada Lovelace] gave birth
  to the modern concept of a function.
- The fundamental vocabulary: #strong[preimage (antécédent)],
  #strong[image], #strong[domain of definition] $cal(D)_f$, and the
  ironclad rule of image uniqueness.
- How to construct and interpret a #strong[function curve (graph)], a
  table of values, and a #strong[table of variations].
- The concepts of #strong[maximum], #strong[minimum] (local and global),
  and #strong[parity] (even and odd functions, symmetries in the
  coordinate plane).
- A complete study of the #strong[five parent (reference) functions]:
  the square function ($x^2$), the reciprocal function ($1 / x$), the
  square root function ($sqrt(x)$), the cube function ($x^3$), and the
  absolute value function ($\|x\|$).
- Solving equations $f\(x\)= k$, $f\(x\)= g\(x\)$, and inequalities
  graphically, along with the #strong[composition] of function machines
  $g compose f$.

