=== 4. Parity: Symmetry in the Mirror
<parity-symmetry-in-the-mirror>
==== 4.1 A Domain Centered at the Origin
<a-domain-centered-at-the-origin>
To compare behavior to the left and right of the origin, the domain of
definition must be symmetric with respect to zero:
$ forall x in cal(D)_f\,quad - x in cal(D)_f . $ For instance,
$\[- 3 thin\;3\]$ and $bb(R)\\{ 0 }$ are symmetric about 0; whereas
$\[- 2 thin\;5\]$ is not (for $x = 4$, $- 4$ does not belong to the
set).

==== 4.2 Even and Odd Functions
<even-and-odd-functions>
#principe(title: [Définition Fondamentale])[
#strong[📐 Definition --- Parity.
]
 1. A function $f$ is #strong[even] if
for all $x in cal(D)_f$: $ f\(- x\)= f\(x\). $ #strong[Geometric
property:] Its curve $cal(C)_f$ is #strong[symmetric with respect to the
$y$-axis $\(O y\)$] (reflectional symmetry). 2. A function $f$ is
#strong[odd] if for all $x in cal(D)_f$: $ f\(- x\)= - f\(x\). $
#strong[Geometric property:] Its curve $cal(C)_f$ is #strong[symmetric
with respect to the origin $O$] (half-turn rotational symmetry).
]

