=== 5. The Five Parent Functions
<the-five-parent-functions>
These are the five cornerstone building blocks from which all high
school function machinery is assembled.

==== 5.1 The Square Function: $f\(x\)= x^2$
<the-square-function-fx-x2>
- #strong[Domain of definition:]
  $cal(D)_f = bb(R) =\]- oo thin\;+ oo\[$.
- #strong[Parity:] For every real $x$, $\(- x\)^2 = x^2$. The square
  function is #strong[even].
- #strong[Variations:]
  - On $\]- oo thin\;0\]$, it is strictly decreasing: if
    $a < b lt.eq 0$, then $a^2 > b^2$.

  - On $\[0 thin\;+ oo\[$, it is strictly increasing: if
    $0 lt.eq a < b$, then $a^2 < b^2$.
- #strong[Graph:] An upward-opening #strong[parabola] whose vertex is
  the origin $O\(0 thin\;0\)$. Its absolute minimum is $0$, reached at
  $x = 0$.

