==== 5.3 The Square Root Function: $f\(x\)= sqrt(x)$
<the-square-root-function-fx-sqrtx>
- #strong[Domain of definition:]
  $cal(D)_f =\[0 thin\;+ oo\[= bb(R)_(+)$.

- #strong[Parity:] Meaningless (the domain is not symmetric about 0).

- #strong[Variations:] Strictly increasing on $\[0 thin\;+ oo\[$.
  $ 0 lt.eq a < b arrow.r.double.long sqrt(a) < sqrt(b) . $

- #strong[Graph:] Half-branch of a horizontal parabola. It begins at
  $O\(0 thin\;0\)$ with a vertical tangent at the origin.

==== 5.4 The Cube Function: $f\(x\)= x^3$
<the-cube-function-fx-x3>
- #strong[Domain of definition:] $cal(D)_f = bb(R)$.

- #strong[Parity:] $\(- x\)^3 =\(- 1\)^3 x^3 = - x^3$. The cube function
  is #strong[odd].

- #strong[Variations:] Strictly increasing throughout all of $bb(R)$.
  $ a < b arrow.r.double.long a^3 < b^3 . $

- #strong[Graph:] Crosses the origin with a horizontal inflection point
  at $O\(0 thin\;0\)$.

==== 5.5 The Absolute Value Function: $f\(x\)=\|x\|$
<the-absolute-value-function-fx-x>
- #strong[Domain of definition:] $cal(D)_f = bb(R)$.

- #strong[Piecewise definition:]
  $ \|x\|= cases(delim: "{", x & upright("if ") x gt.eq 0, - x & upright("if ") x < 0) $

- #strong[Parity:] $\|- x\|=\|x\|$. The function is #strong[even].

- #strong[Variations:]

  - Strictly decreasing on $\]- oo thin\;0\]$ (slope $- 1$).

  - Strictly increasing on $\[0 thin\;+ oo\[$ (slope $+ 1$).

- #strong[Graph:] A sharp #strong[V-shape], formed by two rays meeting
  at a right angle at $O\(0 thin\;0\)$. Its absolute minimum is $0$.

