=== Key Takeaways
<key-takeaways-15>
+ #strong[Function:] $x mapsto f\(x\)$. To every preimage
  $x in cal(D)_f$ corresponds #strong[exactly one image] $f\(x\)$. A
  number may have $0$, $1$, or multiple preimages.

+ #strong[Domain $cal(D)_f$:]

  - Denominator $eq.not 0$.
  - Quantity inside a square root $gt.eq 0$.

+ #strong[Variations:]

  - Increasing: $a < b arrow.r.double.long f\(a\)lt.eq f\(b\)$
    (preserves order).
  - Decreasing: $a < b arrow.r.double.long f\(a\)gt.eq f\(b\)$ (reverses
    order).

+ #strong[Parity:]

  - Even: $f\(- x\)= f\(x\)$, line symmetry across $y$-axis $\(O y\)$.
  - Odd: $f\(- x\)= - f\(x\)$, rotational point symmetry about origin
    $O$.

+ #strong[The 5 Parent Functions:]

  - Square $x^2$: $cal(D) = bb(R)$, even, decreasing on $bb(R)_(-)$,
    increasing on $bb(R)_(+)$, vertex $O\(0 thin\;0\)$.

  - Reciprocal $1 / x$: $cal(D) = bb(R)^(*)$, odd, decreasing on
    $\]- oo thin\;0\[$ and on $\]0 thin\;+ oo\[$.

  - Square root $sqrt(x)$: $cal(D) =\[0 thin\;+ oo\[$, increasing.

  - Cube $x^3$: $cal(D) = bb(R)$, odd, increasing.

  - Absolute value $\|x\|$: $cal(D) = bb(R)$, even, V-shaped.

+ #strong[Graphical Solution:] $f\(x\)= k$ $arrow.l.r.double$
  $x$-coordinates of points where curve crosses horizontal height $k$.

