=== Key Takeaways
<key-takeaways-16>
+ #strong[Standard Form:] $f\(x\)= a x^2 + b x + c$ ($a eq.not 0$).

+ #strong[Canonical (Vertex) Form:] $f\(x\)= a\(x - alpha\)^2 + beta$
  where:
  $ alpha = - frac(b, 2 a) quad upright("and") quad beta = f\(alpha\)= - frac(Delta, 4 a) . $

  - Vertex of the parabola: $S\(alpha\,beta\)$.

  - Axis of symmetry: line $x = alpha$.

  - Opens upward if $a > 0$ (minimum $beta$), opens downward if $a < 0$
    (maximum $beta$).

+ #strong[Discriminant $Delta = b^2 - 4 a c$:]

  - $Delta > 0$: 2 distinct real roots
    $x_1 = frac(- b - sqrt(Delta), 2 a)$ and
    $x_2 = frac(- b + sqrt(Delta), 2 a)$.

  - $Delta = 0$: 1 double real root $x_0 = - frac(b, 2 a)$.

  - $Delta < 0$: 0 real roots.

+ #strong[Factored Form:]

  - If $Delta > 0$: $a\(x - x_1\)\(x - x_2\)$.
  - If $Delta = 0$: $a\(x - x_0\)^2$.

+ #strong[Sign of the Trinomial:]

  - Always of the same sign as $a$, #strong[except between the roots]
    (if $Delta > 0$) where it takes the sign of $- a$.

+ #strong[Viète's Formulas:]
  $ S = x_1 + x_2 = - b / a\,quad P = x_1 x_2 = c / a\,quad X^2 - S X + P = 0 . $

