=== The Question Opening the Next Stage
<the-question-opening-the-next-stage>
The quadratic degree has taught us to predict the continuous arch of a
water jet soaring through space. But in the physical world, not all
phenomena flow like a continuous stream:

- A bank account yields interest at the end of each discrete month;
- A bacterial colony doubles with every passing hour;
- A staircase is climbed step by step, $0\,1\,2\,3 dots.h$

How can we study a quantity that progresses in discrete jumps through
time? How can we calculate the sum of a thousand steps without
exhaustion? This is what we will discover in #strong[The Staircase Steps
and the Usurer's Loan].

