=== The Question Opening the Next Stage
<the-question-opening-the-next-stage-1>
In this chapter, we explored sequences advancing by discrete strides,
and we computed quantities that cycle or oscillate. But now imagine a
fairground Ferris wheel spinning endlessly, or an ocean wave rising and
falling with rhythmic perfection.

How can we measure angles not in rigid degrees, but by unwinding a
flexible ribbon around a circle of radius 1? How do cosine and sine,
first discovered in middle school right-angled triangles, become the
undulations of waves describing sound, light, and alternating electric
current? This is what we will discover in #strong[The Ferris Wheel and
the Winding Circle].

