=== What You Are About to Discover
<what-you-are-about-to-discover-36>
- Why the #strong[degree] is no longer sufficient when we want to
  describe motion that turns endlessly (wheels, planets, waves, motors).
- A new unit of angle, born from the circle itself: the #strong[radian].
- How to #strong[wind the real number line] around a circle of radius 1,
  and thereby give meaning to $cos\(100\)$, to $sin\(- 7\)$, or to
  $cos (frac(37 pi, 4))$.
- The #strong[special values] ($pi / 6\,pi / 4\,pi / 3$) proved with a
  square and an equilateral triangle.
- The #strong[associated angles]: how the symmetries of the circle allow
  everything to be brought back to the first quadrant.
- How to #strong[solve] the equations $cos x = a$ and $sin x = a$, and
  sketch the undulating curves of the cosine and sine functions.

