=== The Question Opening the Next Stage
<the-question-opening-the-next-stage-2>
The scalar product has enabled us to measure the inclination of a force
relative to a straight path, and to calculate the slope of a rigid
segment. What happens, however, when the slope is no longer a straight
line, but an #strong[undulating curve] like a snow-covered hill down
which a skier hurtles at full speed? How can we measure the tilt of the
ski beneath the skier's boots at an infinitesimal instant, at a single
point of contact? This is the great adventure of
#strong[differentiation], which opens in the next chapter.

