=== 1. The Problem: The Petri Dish and the Biological Clock
<the-problem-the-petri-dish-and-the-biological-clock>
Peer through the eyepiece of a microscope in a biology laboratory. In a
Petri dish filled with nutrient agar, a researcher deposits at noon
($t = 0$) a single bacterium of #emph[Escherichia coli].

This bacterium feeds. After twenty minutes, it elongates and splits into
two: there are 2 bacteria. Twenty minutes later, each divides in turn:
there are 4 bacteria. Then 8, then 16, 32, 64, 128, 256…

#align(center)[
  #block(
    fill: rgb("#f8fafc"),
