#strong[Detailed Solution:] Total count:
$N = 2 + 4 + 6 + 5 + 2 + 1 = 20$. 1. Mean:
$ sum n_i x_i =\(2 times 6\)+\(4 times 8\)+\(6 times 10\)+\(5 times 12\)+\(2 times 15\)+\(1 times 18\) $
$ = 12 + 32 + 60 + 60 + 30 + 18 = 212 . $
$ macron(x) = 212 / 20 = 10.6 . $

#block[
#set enum(numbering: "1.", start: 2)
+ König-Huygens formula for variance: Compute $sum n_i x_i^2$:
  $ 2\(36\)+ 4\(64\)+ 6\(100\)+ 5\(144\)+ 2\(225\)+ 1\(324\) $
  $ = 72 + 256 + 600 + 720 + 450 + 324 = 2422 . $
  $ overline(x^2) = 2422 / 20 = 121.1 . $
  $ V = overline(x^2) -\(macron(x)\)^2 = 121.1 -\(10.6\)^2 = 121.1 - 112.36 = 8.74 . $

+ Standard deviation: $ sigma = sqrt(V) = sqrt(8.74) approx 2.96 . $ The
  class average is $10.6$ with a standard deviation of nearly $3$
  points.
]
]

#quote_box[
#strong[✅ Worked Example 2 --- Determining Median and Quartiles
]
 Find
$M_e$, $Q_1$, $Q_3$, and the $I Q R$ for the dataset in Example 1.

