=== What You Must Remember
<what-you-must-remember-10>
+ #strong[Measures of Central Tendency:]

  - Mean: $macron(x) = 1 / N sum n_i x_i = sum f_i x_i$. Highly
    sensitive to extreme values.

  - Median $M_e$: middle value (50% above, 50% below). Robust against
    outliers.

  - Quartiles: $Q_1$ (at least 25%) and $Q_3$ (at least 75%).

+ #strong[Measures of Dispersion:]

  - Interquartile range: $I Q R = Q_3 - Q_1$.

  - Variance: $V = 1 / N sum n_i\(x_i - macron(x)\)^2$.

  - König-Huygens formula:
    $#box(stroke: black, inset: 3pt, [$ V = overline(x^2) -\(macron(x)\)^2 $])$.

  - Standard deviation:
    $#box(stroke: black, inset: 3pt, [$ sigma = sqrt(V) $])$ (shares
    original units of the data).

+ #strong[Affine Transformations ($y = a x + b$):]

  - $macron(y) = a macron(x) + b$

  - $V\(a X + b\)= a^2 V\(X\)$

  - $sigma\(a X + b\)=\|a\|sigma\(X\)$

+ #strong[Sampling and Fluctuation (at 95% Confidence):]

  - $I_0.95 = [p - 1.96 sqrt(frac(p\(1 - p\), n)) med \; med p + 1.96 sqrt(frac(p\(1 - p\), n))]$
    (for $n gt.eq 30$, $n p gt.eq 5$, $n\(1 - p\)gt.eq 5$).
  - If observed sample frequency $f in.not I_0.95$, reject hypothesis
    $p$.

