#strong[\16.] Let $S_1 = sum_(x in G_1) x^2$ and
$S_2 = sum_(x in G_2) x^2$. By König-Huygens in each group:
$S_1 = N_1\(V_1 + macron(x)_1^2\)$ and
$S_2 = N_2\(V_2 + macron(x)_2^2\)$. In the pooled group:
$macron(x) = frac(N_1 macron(x)_1 + N_2 macron(x)_2, N)$, and
