=== Key Takeaways
<key-takeaways-19>
+ #strong[Definition of convergence:] $lim u_n = L$ means that every
  open interval containing $L$ contains all terms of the sequence from a
  rank $N$ onward.

+ #strong[Divergence toward $+ oo$:] every interval $\]A\;+ oo\[$
  contains all terms of the sequence from a certain rank onward.

+ #strong[Indeterminate Forms:] $oo - oo$, $0 times oo$, $oo / oo$,
  $0 / 0$. For a quotient of polynomials in $n$, always factor out the
  highest-degree term in both the numerator and the denominator.

+ #strong[Squeeze Theorem:] If $v_n lt.eq u_n lt.eq w_n$ and
  $lim v_n = lim w_n = L$, then $lim u_n = L$.

+ #strong[Comparison Theorem:] If $u_n gt.eq v_n$ and $lim v_n = + oo$,
  then $lim u_n = + oo$.

+ #strong[Geometric Sequences $q^n$:]

  - If $q > 1$, $lim q^n = + oo$ (proven via Bernoulli's inequality
    $\(1 + a\)^n gt.eq 1 + n a$).

  - If $- 1 < q < 1$, $lim q^n = 0$.

  - If $q lt.eq - 1$, no limit.

+ #strong[Monotone Convergence:] Increasing $+$ bounded above
  $arrow.r.double.long$ convergent. Decreasing $+$ bounded below
  $arrow.r.double.long$ convergent.

