==== Level  (Guided Reflection and Baccalaureate Style)
<level-guided-reflection-and-baccalaureate-style-1>
#strong[Exercise 45.9 (Baccalaureate Style: Function Study with
Exponential).] Consider the function $f$ defined on $bb(R)$ by:
$ f\(x\)=\(x - 2\)e^x + x . $ 1. Determine the limit of $f$ at $- oo$.
\2. Prove that the line $\(Delta\)$ with equation $y = x$ is an oblique
asymptote to the curve $cal(C)_f$ at $- oo$. 3. Determine the relative
position of $cal(C)_f$ with respect to $\(Delta\)$ on
$\]- oo thin\;thin + oo\[$. 4. Determine the limit of $f$ at $+ oo$.

