== CHAPTER 46: The Unbroken Thread
<chapter-46-the-unbroken-thread>
#quote_box[
#emph[“Natura non facit saltus --- Nature does not make jumps, said
Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz. If a train leaves Paris at noon and enters
the station in Lyon at two o'clock, it did not vanish at Dijon only to
reappear suddenly fifty kilometers down the line. It pressed against
every meter, every millimeter of track without ever lifting its wheels.
In mathematics, this fidelity to the path is called continuity, and it
possesses the magical power to guarantee that an equation has a solution
even when one is incapable of calculating it by hand.”
]

]

