=== What You Will Discover
<what-you-will-discover-2>
- The driving intuition of #strong[continuity]: a graph drawn in a
  single stroke of the pen without ever lifting the nib from the paper,
  and its formal formulation $lim_(x arrow.r x_0) f\(x\)= f\(x_0\)$.
- Why virtually all functions in physics and natural science are
  continuous, and the crucial implication: #strong[differentiable
  implies continuous] (though the converse is false!).
- The #strong[Intermediate Value Theorem (IVT)]: the absolute certainty
  of crossing a river when traveling from one bank to the other.
- The #strong[corollary of the bijection] (IVT for strictly monotonic
  functions): the \#1 tool on the Baccalaureate exam to prove the
  existence and uniqueness of the solution to an equation $f\(x\)= k$.
- The #strong[bisection method] (dichotomy) for numerical bracketing and
  its implementation in #strong[Python].
- Recurrence sequences $u_(n + 1) = f\(u_n\)$: how the continuity of $f$
  forces the sequence limit to be a #strong[fixed point] ($f\(L\)= L$).

