=== Key Takeaways
<key-takeaways-21>
+ #strong[Continuity at a point:]
  $lim_(x arrow.r x_0) f\(x\)= f\(x_0\)$.
+ #strong[Differentiable implies continuous:] every function
  differentiable on an interval is continuous there. The converse is
  false (e.g., $\|x\|$ at 0).
+ #strong[Intermediate Value Theorem (IVT):] If $f$ is continuous on
  $\[a\;b\]$, it takes every value between $f\(a\)$ and $f\(b\)$ at
  least once.
+ #strong[Bijection Theorem (IVT Corollary):] If $f$ is
  #strong[continuous] and #strong[strictly monotonic] on an interval
  $I$, then the equation $f\(x\)= k$ admits #strong[a unique solution]
  in $I$ for all $k in f\(I\)$.
+ #strong[Bisection method:] interval-halving algorithm to numerically
  bracket a solution with arbitrary precision in a finite number of
  steps.
+ #strong[Fixed point:] If $u_(n + 1) = f\(u_n\)$ with $f$ continuous
  and if $u_n arrow.r L$, then $f\(L\)= L$.

