==== Worked Example 4 --- Tangent Line and Relative Position via Convexity
<worked-example-4-tangent-line-and-relative-position-via-convexity>
#strong[Problem:] Consider the function $f\(x\)=\(2 x - 1\)e^x$ on
$bb(R)$. 1. Compute $f'\(x\)$ and $f''\(x\)$. 2. Prove that $f$ is
convex on $\[- 1 / 2 thin\;thin + oo\[$. 3. Determine the equation of
the tangent line $\(T\)$ to $cal(C)_f$ at the point with abscissa 0. 4.
Deduce the relative position of $cal(C)_f$ with respect to $\(T\)$ on
$\[- 1 / 2 thin\;thin + oo\[$.

#strong[Solution:] 1. #strong[Derivatives:]
$f'\(x\)= 2 e^x +\(2 x - 1\)e^x =\(2 x + 1\)e^x$.
$f''\(x\)= 2 e^x +\(2 x + 1\)e^x =\(2 x + 3\)e^x$. 2.
#strong[Convexity:] Since $e^x > 0$, the sign of $f''\(x\)$ is that of
$2 x + 3$. For all $x gt.eq - 1 / 2$, we have
$2 x + 3 gt.eq 2\(- 1 / 2\)+ 3 = - 1 + 3 = 2 > 0$. Thus
$f''\(x\)gt.eq 0$ on $\[- 1 / 2 thin\;thin + oo\[$, proving that $f$ is
#strong[strictly convex] on this interval. 3. #strong[Tangent at 0:]
$f\(0\)=\(0 - 1\)e^0 = - 1$. $f'\(0\)=\(0 + 1\)e^0 = 1$. The equation of
tangent $\(T\)$ is:
$ y = f'\(0\)\(x - 0\)+ f\(0\)= 1\(x\)- 1 = x - 1 . $ 4.
#strong[Relative position:] Since $f$ is convex on
$\[- 1 / 2 thin\;thin + oo\[$ and the contact point $0$ belongs to this
interval ($0 gt.eq - 1 / 2$), the curve $cal(C)_f$ lies #strong[above
its tangent $\(T\)$] on $\[- 1 / 2 thin\;thin + oo\[$. That is, for all
$x gt.eq - 1 / 2$: $ \(2 x - 1\)e^x gt.eq x - 1 . $

