=== What You Are About to Discover
<what-you-are-about-to-discover-43>
- Why, around 1600, navigators and astronomers were suffocating under
  #strong[multiplications], and how a Scottish baron invented a machine
  to transform multiplications into #strong[additions].
- The #strong[natural logarithm function] $ln$, defined as the machine
  that #strong[undoes] the exponential:
  $y = e^x arrow.l.r.double x = ln y$.
- Its #strong[algebraic properties] ($ln\(a b\)= ln a + ln b$, etc.) and
  their complete #strong[proofs].
- A #strong[comprehensive analysis] of the function: derivative $1 / x$,
  monotonicity, limits, indeterminate forms, asymptotic growth rates,
  and concavity.
- Rigorous methods to solve #strong[equations and inequalities]
  involving $ln$ and $e$, and how to determine #strong[thresholds] in
  geometric sequences.
- Real-world #strong[logarithmic scales]: pH, decibels, earthquake
  magnitudes, and carbon-14 radiometric dating.

