$E = ln\(e^3\)+ ln (1 / e) - ln (e sqrt(e))$.
]
 We have $ln\(e^3\)= 3$,
$ln (1 / e) = - 1$, and $ln (e sqrt(e)) = ln (e^(3\/2)) = 3 / 2$. Thus
