- If $a = e$: $f\(a\)= 1 / e$ is the absolute maximum; the equation has
  the unique solution $x = e$.

- If $a > 1$ and $a eq.not e$: the value
  $f\(a\)in ]0 thin \; 1 / e[$ is attained at exactly two points:
  one in $\]1 thin\;e\[$ and one in $\]e thin\;+ oo\[$. One solution is
