=== The Question that Opens What Follows
<the-question-that-opens-what-follows-15>
The logarithm and exponential functions allow us to master growth that
explodes without bound and decay that fades toward zero. But in the
physical universe, not everything grows or vanishes indefinitely: the
seasons repeat, the heart beats, planets orbit, guitar strings vibrate,
and a child's swing rocks back and forth.

How do mathematics describe phenomena that #strong[return endlessly to
their starting point]? How do we calculate the instantaneous velocity of
a pendulum at the exact instant it swings through its lowest point?

Welcome to the world of oscillations, waves, and the geometry of the
circle: join us in Chapter 49 with #strong[The Swing and Oscillating
Functions].

