$cos x gt.eq 0 arrow.r.double.long cos''\(x\)lt.eq 0$: the function is
#strong[concave]. On $[pi / 2 thin \; pi]$,
$cos x lt.eq 0 arrow.r.double.long cos''\(x\)gt.eq 0$: the function is
#strong[convex]. An inflection point occurs at $x = pi / 2$, where the
curve crosses the horizontal axis with a slope of $- 1$.

==== 4.2 Analysis of the Sine Function
<analysis-of-the-sine-function>
On the interval $\[0 thin\;pi\]$:

- $sin'\(x\)= cos x$.
- On $[0 thin \; pi / 2]$, $cos x > 0$: $sin$ is #strong[strictly
  increasing].
- At $x = pi / 2$, $cos (pi / 2) = 0$: horizontal tangent at
  $(pi / 2 thin \; 1)$.
- On $]pi / 2 thin \; pi[$, $cos x < 0$: $sin$ is #strong[strictly
  decreasing].

