#strong[Solution 49.20:] Assume for contradiction that
$lim_(x arrow.r + oo) cos x = L$. By the sequential characterization of
limits, for every sequence $\(u_n\)$ such that $u_n arrow.r + oo$, we
must have $cos\(u_n\)arrow.r L$. Choose $u_n = 2 n pi arrow.r + oo$.
