an open desert. Your odometer is broken: it permanently reads
$0 upright(" km")$. However, your speedometer functions flawlessly, and
a continuous chart recorder plots your instantaneous speed $v\(t\)$ in
kilometers per hour as time $t$ progresses.

How can you determine the exact total distance traveled between
departure at time $t = a$ and arrival at time $t = b$?

+ #strong[The Case of Constant Velocity:] If you cruise at a steady
  speed of $90 upright(" km/h")$ for $2 upright(" hours")$, the distance
  is:
