=== Key Takeaways
<key-takeaways-25>
==== 1. The Definite Integral
<the-definite-integral>
- $integral_a^b f\(t\)thin d t$ represents the signed algebraic area
  enclosed between the graph of $f$, the horizontal axis, and the
  vertical lines $x = a$ and $x = b$.
- The unit of area (u.a.) is the area of the unit coordinate cell
  $parallel arrow(i) parallel times parallel arrow(j) parallel$.

==== 2. The Fundamental Theorem of Calculus
<the-fundamental-theorem-of-calculus>
- If $f$ is continuous on $I$ and $a in I$, the function
  $A\(x\)= integral_a^x f\(t\)thin d t$ is differentiable on $I$ and
  #strong[$A'\(x\)= f\(x\)$].
- For any antiderivative $F$ of $f$ on $\[a thin\;b\]$:
  $ integral_a^b f\(t\)thin d t =\[F\(t\)\]_a^b = F\(b\)- F\(a\). $

==== 3. Standard Antiderivatives Summary
<standard-antiderivatives-summary>
- $x^n arrow.r frac(x^(n + 1), n + 1) quad\(n eq.not - 1\)$
- $1 / x arrow.r ln\|x\|$
- $e^(a x) arrow.r 1 / a e^(a x)$
- $cos\(a x\)arrow.r 1 / a sin\(a x\)$ and
  $sin\(a x\)arrow.r - 1 / a cos\(a x\)$
- $u' u^n arrow.r frac(u^(n + 1), n + 1)$
- $u' / u arrow.r ln\|u\|$
- $u' e^u arrow.r e^u$

==== 4. Key Properties
<key-properties>
- Linearity:
  $integral\(alpha f + beta g\)= alpha integral f + beta integral g$.
- Chasles' relation: $integral_a^c f + integral_c^b f = integral_a^b f$.
- Positivity: if $a lt.eq b$ and $f gt.eq 0$, then
  $integral_a^b f gt.eq 0$.
- Area between curves: $cal(A) = integral_a^b\(f\(x\)- g\(x\)\)thin d x$
  whenever $f gt.eq g$.
- Mean value: $mu = frac(1, b - a) integral_a^b f\(t\)thin d t$.

==== 5. Integration by Parts
<integration-by-parts>
$ integral_a^b u' v =\[u v\]_a^b - integral_a^b u v' . $

