=== The Question that Opens What Follows
<the-question-that-opens-what-follows-17>
We now know how to compute the area under a curve whenever an explicit
formula for the function is known. But what happens in the real world,
when we do not know the formula of the function in advance, but only
#strong[a relationship linking the function to its own rate of change]?

When a hot cup of tea sits on a kitchen table, the rate at which it
cools is directly proportional to the difference between its temperature
and the ambient room temperature. How can we uncover the complete
temperature profile over time from this simple physical rule?

Welcome to the realm of #strong[differential equations]: join us in
Chapter 51 with #strong[The Cooling Cup of Tea].

