<what-you-are-about-to-discover-47>
- How cathedral builders conquered the #strong[third dimension]: from
  the flat ground to the celestial keystone.
- The orthonormal coordinate system
  $\(O\;arrow(i)\,arrow(j)\,arrow(k)\)$ of 3D space: abscissa ($x$),
  ordinate ($y$), #strong[z-coordinate / altitude] ($z$), and the 3D
  distance formula derived from a double Pythagorean theorem.
- The #strong[parametric representation of a line] in space: why a line
  in 3D can never be described by a single Cartesian equation.
