=== The Question That Opens the Next Step
<the-question-that-opens-the-next-step>
We have learned to measure continuous space: lengths, angles, flat
surfaces, and 3D volumes. Yet the mathematical universe is not limited
to geometric continua. It is equally built upon discrete choices: How
many paths lead from one vertex to another? How many possible
combinations on a bicycle lock with dials? In how many ways can one
choose 5 cards from a deck of 32, or assemble a committee of delegates?

How can we count without ever enumerating one by one toward infinity?

See you in Chapter 53 with #strong[the combination lock and ways of
choosing].

