=== 7. Geometric Applications: Distances, Angles, and Transformations
<geometric-applications-distances-angles-and-transformations>
==== 7.1 Affixes, Distances, and Oriented Angles
<affixes-distances-and-oriented-angles>
In the complex plane equipped with an orthonormal frame
$\(O\;arrow(u)\,arrow(v)\)$:

- To every point $M\(x\,y\)$ or vector $arrow(V)\(x\,y\)$, we associate
  its #strong[affix (complex coordinate)] $z = x + i y$.
- The vector $accent(A B, ⃗)$ has affix $z_(accent(A B, ⃗)) = z_B - z_A$.
- The #strong[distance] $A B$ is the modulus:
  $ A B = parallel accent(A B, ⃗) parallel =\|z_B - z_A\| $

#quote_box[
#strong[📐 Theorem --- Oriented Angle Between Two Vectors
]
 For any four
points $A\,B\,C\,D$ with $A eq.not B$ and $C eq.not D$:
$ \(accent(A B, ⃗)\,accent(C D, ⃗)\)equiv arg (frac(z_D - z_C, z_B - z_A)) med\(mod med 2 pi\) $
]

==== 7.2 Collinearity and Orthogonality Criteria
<collinearity-and-orthogonality-criteria>
Define the ratio $Z = frac(z_C - z_A, z_B - z_A)$:

- #strong[Collinear Points (Alignment):] Points $A\,B\,C$ are collinear
  if and only if the angle $\(accent(A B, ⃗)\,accent(A C, ⃗)\)$ equals $0$
  or $pi$ modulo $2 pi$:
  $ A\,B\,C upright(" collinear") arrow.l.r.double frac(z_C - z_A, z_B - z_A) in bb(R) $

- #strong[Perpendicular Lines (Orthogonality):] Lines $\(A B\)$ and
  $\(C D\)$ are perpendicular if and only if the angle
  $\(accent(A B, ⃗)\,accent(C D, ⃗)\)$ equals $plus.minus pi / 2$ modulo
  $2 pi$:
  $ \(A B\)perp\(C D\)arrow.l.r.double frac(z_D - z_C, z_B - z_A) in i bb(R) quad (upright("purely imaginary")) $

==== 7.3 Plane Transformations via Complex Numbers
<plane-transformations-via-complex-numbers>
