=== The Question That Opens the Future
<the-question-that-opens-the-future-4>
We have just seen how arithmetic equations allow us to encrypt
information flows and link integer variables. But what happens when the
flows to be transformed are no longer isolated numbers, but entire
tables of data, interconnected networks, and probabilistic states in
perpetual transition? How do we model the evolution of a population, the
ranking of web pages by Google, or the states of a Turing machine? To
orchestrate these multidimensional flows, mathematicians forged a
spectacular tool: matrices and graphs. Turn the page to discover
#strong[Chapter 57 and The Jacquard Loom Revisited: Matrices and
Graphs].

