=== What to Remember from High School
<what-to-remember-from-high-school>
+ #strong[The Derivative $f'\(a\)$:] Slope of the tangent line,
  instantaneous rate of change. Governs variations, extrema, and
  convexity.

+ #strong[The Integral $integral_a^b f\(x\)d x$:] Area under the curve,
  continuous summation. Linked to differentiation by the Fundamental
  Theorem of Calculus: $integral_a^b f\(t\)d t = F\(b\)- F\(a\)$.

+ #strong[The Exponential $e^x$ and the Logarithm $ln x$:] The function
  identical to its own derivative ($y' = y$) and its inverse. They
  govern biological growth and physical scaling laws.

+ #strong[Vectors and the Dot Product:]
  $arrow(u) dot.op arrow(v) = parallel arrow(u) parallel parallel arrow(v) parallel cos theta = x x' + y y' + z z'$.
  The master tool for orthogonality and projections.

+ #strong[Complex Numbers $bb(C)$:] $z = a + i b = r e^(i theta)$, with
  $i^2 = - 1$. The seamless synthesis of algebra and planar rotations.

+ #strong[Combinatorics and Probability:] $binom(n, k)$, the binomial
  distribution $cal(B)\(n\,p\)$, and the Law of Large Numbers:
  individual randomness surrenders to collective order.

+ #strong[Arithmetic and Matrices:] Congruences modulo $n$, Bézout's
  identity, graphs and Markov chains $P_(n + 1) = P_n times T$.

